  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Fast-break waves – 3 v 2 into 2 v 1",
  "description": "Full court. Two defenders wait at one basket, one close to the rim and one up at the free-throw line. Three attackers start from the other half: one in the middle with the ball and one in each outside lane. They push the break 3 v 2 and try to score quickly.\n\nWhen the 3 v 2 ends – score, miss or turnover – the two defenders take the ball and go 2 v 1 the other way. The player who took the shot in the 3 v 2 sprints back and defends alone. The other two attackers stay and become the new defenders at that basket.\n\nAfter the 2 v 1 those three go to the lines on the baseline, and the next group of three starts a new 3 v 2 against the two who are waiting. The drill never stops. Progression: a shot clock on each attack, or compete for the most baskets in five minutes.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Fill the lanes: stay wide near the sidelines and run all the way."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Middle ball-handler draws a defender, then passes – decide before the free-throw line."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defence in the 3 v 2: the top player stops the ball, the back player takes the first pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The shooter turns at once and sprints back – you are the only defender."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
